  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MHPSS Specialist with UNHCR in Peru</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2018, the United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees (UNHCR) and the International Organization for Migration (IOM) have coordinated the implementation of the necessary actions to support and complement the response of responses of 17 countries&apos; governments to the protection and assistance needs of Venezuelans within the framework of the Regional Response Plan for Refugees and Migrants (RMRP).Peru is the second country, following Colombia, as of December 2022, there were 1,078,854 individuals of Venezuelan nationality in Peru, constituting 21% of the total Venezuelan refugee and migrant population.The Working Group for Refugees and Migrants is responsible for the implementation of the Peru Chapter of the RMRP. The purpose of promoting lasting solutions in the psychosocial adjustment of refugees and migrants is based on the comprehensive implementation of various protection and mental health and psychosocial support services. The support of a surge support expert in MHPSS is important to revitalise the national level group and strengthen the involvement of all stakeholders for better coordination of actions across the country.</narrative>
  </description>
